==Scots==

===Etymology===
{{OE.}} {{term|maþa|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic|maþa-|worm|lang=sco}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|math-||moth-|used for insects and vermin|lang=sco}}.  Cognate with Dutch {{term|made|lang=nl}}, German {{term|Made|lang=de}} and related to Swedish {{term|mask|lang=sv}}, Danish {{term|madike|lang=da}}, archaic English {{term|maddock}} (English {{term|maggot}}).

